OL,3,GNEWSAThe engineers using WW2 skills to
OL,4,Akeep historic planes in the air
OL,5,
OL,6,FAn RAF engineer who is part of the team
OL,7,Fkeeping the Battle of Britain Memorial
OL,8,FFlight planes in the air says his job
OL,9,Finvolves using skills from a bygone
OL,10,Fera.
OL,12,FSgt Rob Taylor, based at RAF Coningsby
OL,13,Fin Lincolnshire, helps keep aircraft
OL,14,Fincluding a Lancaster bomber, a Dakota,
OL,15,FSpitfires and Hurricanes airworthy for
OL,16,Fdisplays and commemorative events.
OL,18,FTaylor said engineers often relied on
OL,19,Fmanuals dating back to 1945, which
OL,20,Fassumed levels of knowledge and
OL,21,Fexperience that were no longer taught.
OL,23,APub: 20-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,387,380,200,160,0,100
